            "stmt_text": "\tkfree(isw);",
            "location": "context",
            "explanation": "This kfree() call frees the isw structure during inode writeback switching. Without proper synchronization or reference counting verification, this could lead to use-after-free vulnerabilities if other code paths still hold references to isw or access it concurrently. The surrounding code handles inode writeback with wb_get/iput reference counting and RCU protection, making premature or unprotected deallocation of isw a potential race condition vector."
